From a1151698062e3db11ad37589180760f6100acadb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:19:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] B70-Q27-0004: native XPU int8 act quant + oneDNN W8A8
 int8 GEMM when the kernels wheel has them

Activation quant: ops.scaled_int8_quant (W8A8) and xpu_ops.dynamic_per_token_int8_quant
(INC w4a8, XPUW4A8IntLinearKernel) call _C::dynamic_per_token_scaled_int8_quant when the
vllm-xpu-kernels wheel registers it (0.1.16.2+gv.pr660662.int8n.*), else the torch.compile
reference as before. Same bits either way. Decided once at import (B70_XPU_INT8_QUANT_NATIVE=0
forces the reference); logs "B70 int8 act-quant: native op".

W8A8 GEMM: XPUInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel (oneDNN _xpu_C::int8_scaled_mm) ahead of
TritonInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel on XPU, selected only with B70_XPU_INT8_ONEDNN=1 and the op
present; symmetric activations only (asymmetric stays on Triton). Logs "B70 int8 GEMM: oneDNN".
